# Testing and Quality

## Required coverage areas

- Unit tests for services, selectors, and policies
- Integration tests for multi-model workflows
- Authorization tests for deny-by-default and scoped roles
- Workflow tests for submit/check/verify/amend paths
- PostgreSQL transaction tests for multi-record operations
- Browser end-to-end tests with Playwright for critical journeys
- Security-focused tests for authentication and privilege boundaries

## Tools

- Pytest for automated backend tests
- Playwright for browser end-to-end tests
- GitHub Actions for CI when workflows are introduced

## Quality bar

- Every security and workflow rule must have tests.
- Do not claim production readiness without UAT, restore testing, security review, and owner approval.
- Test evidence must be traceable to requirement IDs where requirements exist.
- Deviations must be recorded; they do not silently become accepted behavior.
